(c)(1) In the preparation of a form that requires identification of individuals by  race, a department or independent unit shall include the following racial categories:

(i) American Indian or Alaska Native;

(ii) Asian;

(iii) Black or African American;

(iv) Native Hawaiian or other Pacific Islander; and

(v) White.

(2) A form that requires identification of individuals by race shall include instructions  that multiracial respondents may select all applicable racial categories.

(3)(i) Respondents shall select their own answers, except when it is not possible  for the respondent to do so.

